      "source": [
        "### Cell 11: Choosing X - pairwise correlation and VIF\n",
        "VIF measures how much a variable is explained by the other variables (VIF > 10 is a sign of severe multicollinearity). Computed on the **train set** (missing values imputed with the train median).\n",
        "Selection rule: keep a variable if VIF <= 10; if a pair of variables is too highly correlated (|r| > 0.7), consider dropping one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 14,
      "id": "e09666b8",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
